# Milestone report format

At the end of every milestone, display the complete report directly in chat.

## One block

Put the entire report in one fenced plain-text code block. Use a `text` fence.

- Start the block with the milestone line and title:

  RELIEF FORGE — MILESTONE X.X.X
  MILESTONE TITLE

- Include every section (A, B, C, and so on) in that same block.
- Keep SHA-256 hashes, measurements, comparisons, errors, and limitations in the block.
- The whole report must be copyable with one copy action.

## Do not

- Do not use HTML `<details>` tags.
- Do not write a separate Markdown report file.
- Do not link to a report.
- Do not use more than one code block.
- Do not substitute a short summary for the full report.
- Do not add text before or after the block unless there is a critical blocker.
- Do not write or change anything under `projects/` to store or format the report.

## Collapse

The Cursor interface may collapse a long code block. This rule cannot set that collapse state. Do not claim the block was collapsed programmatically. Still output the complete report in the one block.
